## Unified Nornir Logging Convention

All Nornir Python projects write persistent logs through one convention owned by `nornir-shared`.

- Initialize persistent logging with `nornir_shared.misc.SetupLogging`; `NORNIR_LOG_ROOT` is the file-log root.
- Do not hardcode absolute log paths in modules or create ad hoc debug files (`debug-*.log`, repo-root logs, per-project log directories).
- Put project identity in logger names / record content, not in per-project file names.
- `nornir_shared.misc` owns log location and naming; `nornir_shared.prettyoutput` is presentation-layer output and must not own file sink paths.

### Session layout

With `NORNIR_LOG_ROOT` set, log files follow:

- `<NORNIR_LOG_ROOT>/<YYYY-MM-DD>/nornir-session-<YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS>.log`
- `<NORNIR_LOG_ROOT>/<YYYY-MM-DD>/nornir-session-<YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS>-errors.log`

The parent creates one session ID; child processes in the same run reuse it.

### Multiprocessing

- Parent: `nornir_shared.misc.StartMultiprocessLoggingListener(...)` before creating workers; `nornir_shared.misc.StopMultiprocessLoggingListener()` on shutdown.
- Workers: `nornir_shared.misc.ConfigureWorkerQueueLogging(...)` so they emit through `QueueHandler`. Do not attach file handlers directly in workers.
